            "result_text": "Done! I successfully extracted the secret key from the vulnerable program.\n\n**The vulnerability:** The program uses an unsafe `gets()` function that doesn't check buffer bounds. It allocates a 0x40-byte buffer on the stack and then checks if a value at offset 0x40 (immediately after the buffer) equals 1.\n\n**The exploit:** By sending a payload of 0x40 bytes followed by a single byte with value 0x01, I triggered a buffer overflow that sets the authentication check flag to 1, bypassing the security check and revealing the encrypted secret, which the program then decrypts.\n\n**Result:** The secret key `FLAG{b4ff3r_0v3rfl0w_m4st3r_k3y_2024}` has been extracted and saved to `/app/results.txt`."
